    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:fb5db666cae6efb7",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "f261ec5f1176743d3b8aff190ccf820438f8991f46c776a423e2849e715b75c8",
      "text": "Day 8 · Santiago enjoys some of the most striking scenery in Latin America, with the Andes rising above a city of skyscrapers that stretches as far as the eye can see. After breakfast, tour the historic centre, beginning at the Plaza de Armas, the city’s central hub since colonial times, where you can imagine the bustling markets, merchants and soldiers of the past.\n\nThe square is home to several monuments, including that of Pedro de Valdivia, founder of Santiago, as well as the Palace of the Royal Audience, the Metropolitan Cathedral and the Central Post Office. After the excursion, transfer back to the hotel.\n\nOptional: wine-tasting tour to the wineries of the Maipo Valley (USD 276 per person, minimum 2 people).",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1X7vYrKfJejOIcKnAqLzOpNNqMi_FS0Mx",
        "documentSha256": "d6a0fea61270c4c20d307d3029b9c8fc090134a96b082cedfc3ed496b503946f",
